# fonts: Fix the Tahoma bitmap strike glyphs that are broken or too wide.
# https://gitlab.winehq.org/wine/wine/-/merge_requests/12715 state=merged
# A few Tahoma strike glyphs are only a dot instead of the glyph: the 9 pixel U+02DD, the 13, 15 and 16 pixel U+2018 and the 15 pixel U+00EC; draw them from the outline instead. The 8 pixel Cyrillic glyphs do not fit the strike: the small letters are 5 pixels high instead of 4 like the Latin ones and most of them are one column wider than on Windows, so that nearly all the letter pairs touch; redraw them on the grid of the Latin glyphs. A few other glyphs per size are one column wider than on Windows at the same advance width; make them one column narrower.

Tahoma 8-16 pixels, no antialiasing:

![tahoma-strike-glyphs-mr-en](/uploads/e7fd8f99bc047d72c8412f757e07cd1c/tahoma-strike-glyphs-mr-en.png)

Wine-Bug: https://bugs.winehq.org/show_bug.cgi?id=60741
